    "note": "**v1 PROD GATE \u2014 `@m0saic/dsl-tutorial/v1` \"DSL Tutorial\"** (gate 33 \u2014 the north-star polish benchmark; load-bearing since gate 30 deprecated the animated wireframe in its favour; chart: `.ai/LAUNCH/v1-template-cut.md`). Core tier, tags dsl-tutorial \u00b7 tutorial \u00b7 wireframe \u00b7 docs \u00b7 animated. Props = pure defaults \u2192 the 2\u00d72 walk, light preset, **15.8s natural** (was 12s: see finding 1).\n\nYour heads-up (\"text clipping \u2014 we should have debug layout guards\") drove the pre-audit. The engine's drawtext never shrinks a string (`fit:\"contain\"` only picks the anchor), and every font in the tutorial scaled from the bar HEIGHT alone \u2014 so anything narrower than 16:9 clipped: on 1080\u00d71920 the title read \"Animated\", the pills \"ed 1\" / \"p 10 /\", the inspector \"INSF\" / \"60\" (for 960) / \"80\" (for 1080) / \"ENGIN\", and every status metric was cut mid-word.\n\n| Stage | Current | Proposed |\n|---|---|---|\n| Flags | core \u00b7 not internal \u00b7 not deprecated | confirm |\n| Label | \"DSL Tutorial\" | keep |\n| Header title default | was \"Animated Wireframe\" (the deprecated sibling's name) | **\"DSL Tutorial\"** \u2014 revertable, one line |\n| Duration | the 12s outputHint was read as a PIN \u2192 every walk crammed/stretched to 12s (default ran at 1.3\u00d7; the gallery preview's 61-step walk at 4.7\u00d7) | **Q1 law**: only an explicit ask pins (CLI `--durationMs`, Make Duration). Unpinned = the walk's natural length authored on `durationMs` (~0.9s/char at 1\u00d7); the Speed pill reads 1.0\u00d7 |\n| Cover / Tutorial | none / none | none / none (the template IS a tutorial) |\n| Previews | 07-02 set: \"Animated Wireframe\" header, 4.7\u00d7 crammed walk, strip clipped at both ends | RE-MINT after the verdict (+ corner-M) |\n| Battery | `.scratch/claude/dsl-tutorial-gate-battery.mjs` \u2014 **29/29** (23 CLI renders + ffprobe/pixel asserts: natural / pinned / speed durations, 0 audio streams \u00d723, dark vs light, strip edge columns ink-free, tiny auto-hide + compact pills, portrait app-bar chrome) | \u2014 |\n| Contract sweep | `debugLayout` holds (0 violations) at 1920\u00d71080 \u00b7 1280\u00d7720 \u00b7 1080\u00d71920 \u00b7 1080\u00d71080 \u00b7 3840\u00d72160 \u00b7 960\u00d7540 \u00b7 800\u00d7450 \u00b7 704\u00d7396 \u00b7 640\u00d7360 \u00b7 480\u00d7270 \u00b7 320\u00d7180 \u00b7 1920\u00d7200, plus the 100-tile grid, overlay + passthrough layouts, a long title | \u2014 |\n\n**Pre-audit findings \u2192 fixed:**\n\n| Finding | Fix |\n|---|---|\n| \u2b50 **Text clipped at any non-16:9 canvas** (portrait / square / tiny): title, both pills, inspector caption + chips + 4-digit values + section caption, every status metric | Every string is WIDTH-FITTED under a CLI width model (`_shared/text-fit.ts`, the alpine pack's `textEmUnits \u00d7 em` ruler \u2014 the SAME ruler the contract checks with): the bar height picks the design size, the cell caps it, floors are explicit. Degrade ladders instead of clips: the title ellipsizes at 70% of its design size \u00b7 pills drop to compact wording (`1.0x` \u00b7 `10 / 16`) \u00b7 the status strip drops trailing metrics \u00b7 inspector captions blank at the floor \u00b7 tile dims lines drop when they can't fit at 9px |\n| \u2b50 **No `debugLayout` guard** | `debugLayout` runs `withLayoutContract` THROUGH the nested panels (checkLayout flattens the children): `textFits` on 11 labels (header-title / header-pill / status-label / metric-label / metric-value / narration / inspector-title / chip / field-label / field-value / section-title), each with the em its fit used. On \u2192 the contract wireframe (green = the measured rule) |\n| DSL strip: edge glyphs sat half a column from the panel edge; the flat 1.6\u00b7cellW font cap let `>` (.86em) overlap its neighbours and clip at both ends | the column font is bounded by the WIDEST glyph in the string under a per-glyph m0 model (no overlap, no edge clip); ruler labels likewise |\n| Narration font was height-only \u2192 ran off the right edge on portrait | one font fits the LONGEST line; still-overflowing lines ellipsize at the 10px floor |\n| Chrome rows were % of HEIGHT \u2192 a 173px header slab on portrait | rows size off `min(H, 0.75\u00b7W)` \u2014 landscape byte-identical (9/9/6/70/6), portrait/square get app-bar chrome and hand the rest to the body |\n| Inspector rows filled the panel height \u2192 140px rows with small text on portrait | rows capped at 30% of the panel width, slack at the bottom |\n| \u2b50 **480\u00d7270 CRASHED** (\"expects 39 renderable sources but doc.sources has 40\"): the inspector's section rule = 1/11 of a ~9px band \u2192 a 0-size frame | the rule is quantized at \u22652.5px per unit (a hairline the engine can't zero), captions only below 7px; AND the inspector auto-hides under a 140px slot (canvases < 700px wide \u2014 its 3px cells were never legible) |\n| The contract ITSELF found two more during the sweep: the whole nested layout collapsed (flatten `SPLIT_EXCEEDS_AXIS`) between 700 and 960px wide, and a chip / a pill overshot by 1\u20132px at 800\u00d7450 / 960\u00d7540 \u2014 quantization eats an ABSOLUTE 1\u20132px per split level, not a proportional slice | fit budget = cell \u00d7 0.94 \u2212 2px (`fitBudget`); 12-canvas sweep clean |\n| \u2b50 **CLI `.mosaicx` path never told templates the ask** (`make` / `resolve` built the engine context WITHOUT userIntent): `--durationMs` and the wrapper's `durationMs` set the render length but the template kept its natural timeline \u2192 stress-01 rendered 30s of a 220s walk (TRUNCATED mid-walk, Speed 1.0\u00d7), while Make (which threads its Duration field) rendered the fit | CLI `mosaicxUserIntent` (packages/cli `mosaicxRunner.ts`, 3 locks): the render length reaches templates as userIntent on BOTH paths, so a frozen twin carries the same fitted timeline `make` renders. CLI == Make. (Every self-timing template on the mosaicx path gains this 